/* Frame animation: <nui-frames frames="a.sub, b.sub" delay="0.1"/> or
   <nui-frames pattern="d:/ymir work/ui/x/%02d.sub" count="24" delay="0.05"/>.
   The NovaUI runtime registers the element: it makes one <img> per frame and
   shows one at a time from the clock, so a frame switch rebuilds no mesh;
   reduced motion holds the `rest` frame. The first frame stays in the flow
   and sizes the element; the others are stacked on it, which needs a
   positioned box (docs/ui/AUTHORING.md "Frame animations"). */

nui-frames
{
	display: inline-block;
	position: relative;
}
